#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f1049a-8af9-50ee-9dac-9dbd9c19bdc6" :knowledge-point/title "Correctly Identifying a Scatter Plot"}] :question/id #uuid "b4051787-5d60-53bd-b390-35585ff6ef32" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9679" :question/problem "Johnny wants to find out if there is a relationship between a person's height and their weight. So he records the heights and corresponding weights of some of his classmates. The results are shown in the table below.\n\n| **Height (cm)** | **$165$** | **$170$** | **$170$** | **$175$** | **$180$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Weight (kg)** | $60$ | $70$ | $75$ | $70$ | $75$ |\n\nConstruct a scatter plot that represents this data." :question/worked-solution "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (height) along the horizontal axis.\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (weight) along the vertical axis.\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/630817a152951fe1e8bafba13db730ea.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/id #uuid "35dd0c47-2ee8-57bf-b6c6-65af8ac3c76d" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9680" :question/problem "The scatter plot above shows the relationship between the number of bags of popcorn sold one day and the price per bag at nine locations.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/1db6081814f3b5c2b488e394c39648bb.png)\n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. Only one location sold exactly $10$ bags of popcorn.\n2. Two locations sold bags of popcorn for $\\[math]1.40$ each.\n3. No location sold more than $30$ bags of popcorn." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $10$, namely, $(1.8,10)$. This means only one location sold exactly $10$ bags of popcorn.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/bade3d9c0d8c1087bd40c530f25d7a86.png)\n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $1.4$, namely, $(1.4,30)$. This means that only one location sold popcorn for $\\[math]1.40$ per bag.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/b4c4042789d2ef6a2abe2a17590347c3.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, one location sold more than $30$ bags of popcorn, represented by the dot above the horizontal line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/d4ecff9d77bdc687ca7c3ccb754dc58a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151972 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f99f2aa-f977-5d6e-ae62-a826a897ba9b" :knowledge-point/title "Reading a Scatter Plot"}] :question/id #uuid "0eb6bb49-3b2c-5709-acc8-6a5f78998c89" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9682" :question/problem "A group of $10$ students is surveyed. The scatter plot above shows the relationship between a student's number of hours of sleep per night and their overall grade point average (GPA). How many hours of sleep per night does the student with a GPA of $80\\%$ get?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/a43e082da00d114b014f5b28a8e0bb21.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/f5f13db695eeca6df5ed4ebc336a86f7.png)\n\nTo determine the number of hours of sleep the student with a GPA of $80\\%$ gets, we locate $80$ on the vertical axis and move in the horizontal direction until we find some points, as shown above.\n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(6,80)$. Therefore, the student with a GPA of $80\\%$ sleeps for $6$ hours per night."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3cf74b6-ea62-5325-bbbf-2248a4b7d5de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148945} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd79eea-569b-5697-9417-2ce1dbe46ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148946} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed4260a-7d67-5699-be7e-308b43af2093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148947} {:answer/id #uuid "38304cfe-fc2f-5846-bfc5-de27186897e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148948} {:answer/id #uuid "73eec4d7-ee5f-50a4-88eb-cbc108270aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38304cfe-fc2f-5846-bfc5-de27186897e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148948} :answer-field/id #uuid "b07095f1-cf57-5e8c-a40e-330019508c78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148944}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1109475d-9e0b-5521-b99e-3e1bd3fbb649" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133622" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/q-133622.png)\n\nSarah interviewed some parents, asking them how much time their children spend playing outdoors per day. The information she received is summarized in the scatter plot above.\n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. There is only one child who spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n2. There is only one child aged $6$ among those surveyed.\n3. None of the children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $3.5,$ namely, $(5,3.5).$ This means that only one child spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/0103370189c7156f9677ca576e2480bc99314cd312702fca3ea3e50cb4f7287a.png)\n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $6,$ namely, $(6,2)$ and $(6,2.5).$ This means that there were two children of age $6$ among those surveyed.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/0a8ca9628b48e643e1aa9e9f0216148881db237c2d29054b29f4377ad182503d.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, two children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors. Those children are represented by the two dots below the horizontal line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/4d9709c131045f2e440204f79ad3fd8ff22707312b0e99138da558393e8b7f6d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f1049a-8af9-50ee-9dac-9dbd9c19bdc6" :knowledge-point/title "Correctly Identifying a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eff4db5-5d18-587d-bb96-14249f53b67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/feca9bf417e5b3bf14f65079f8fa2b25e2a7a0f78c5313f4e90bd0070a544722.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247492} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6894ec-1e50-5be3-9e4f-1776992b185d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/cc45b5a8b031e01ad71b93c3e809693c2590c691adb98a2872b47c24839c05f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247493} {:answer/id #uuid "dd31b156-28e8-5039-824a-b134e35e4604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/fcffb96c687ad331dd38bfbb5c3ae5b914c0463ef0fc90e7d354b001b8c693f6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247494} {:answer/id #uuid "6c26266a-604a-54aa-a4e0-c5215870786c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/59c3a4ad97a0de306cf155c6d4094feb1d40dc15daf0898de520a4d7f68a9fc5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247495} {:answer/id #uuid "6d969f84-f8bb-55f2-b14b-f5b92438b032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/ea3821e3b89427494d884fd81deed4a5b052bb811f0d070c678cac4dba708275.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c6894ec-1e50-5be3-9e4f-1776992b185d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/cc45b5a8b031e01ad71b93c3e809693c2590c691adb98a2872b47c24839c05f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247493} :answer-field/id #uuid "01b16d65-6a83-549f-8291-f6a4911f63b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247491}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7859a496-5e4c-591d-9bff-8e93bbc84021" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133963" :question/problem "A coffee shop owner keeps track of how many cups of coffee are sold each morning during the winter, and the temperature at $7$ a.m. each day. The results for the last $5$ days are shown below.\n\n| **Temperature at \n $7$ a.m. (${}^{∘}C$)** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$8$** | **$10$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Cups of Coffee Sold** | $32$ | $28$ | $24$ | $20$ | $16$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?" :question/worked-solution "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows: \n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (the temperature at $7$ a.m.) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (number of cups of coffee sold) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/cc45b5a8b031e01ad71b93c3e809693c2590c691adb98a2872b47c24839c05f7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f1049a-8af9-50ee-9dac-9dbd9c19bdc6" :knowledge-point/title "Correctly Identifying a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "584788f2-e07a-5475-82cc-7028d0491db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/75196d39e72e9ce6ba5b0b32ca486d191bbe209a8a646b030c83b2979fdc3054.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247499} {:answer/id #uuid "04748c80-3cd5-5987-ab74-7612ab022604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/37667e67c6148e8e46c216b1351ada6b16b0e9d3a22de69564415679535fc92e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247500} {:answer/id #uuid "bbdc16d2-3f08-53da-8bea-69876841d929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/58c61701533884a6497bb0e3f692adf4a4d72c648577451fae650dbd164e5001.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247501} {:answer/id #uuid "6f6bdc48-807c-5e28-8d7b-4acef94fcba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/5bdbaadf2d3ea794c145365f5ee61ee4c1551dc72b62c8a681933b9aac74d214.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247502} {:answer/id #uuid "1702e6a1-b856-5453-b0db-d047d88d82af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/d5d7978459fa262b16b4216fa5363a8f14f431e6524163d6e1bbc0f0bdaad7dc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f6bdc48-807c-5e28-8d7b-4acef94fcba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/5bdbaadf2d3ea794c145365f5ee61ee4c1551dc72b62c8a681933b9aac74d214.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247502} :answer-field/id #uuid "28982fba-19a3-5cca-8786-2b661d1b3d64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247498}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "935951a4-ee2a-54bc-9e42-14a72505ef8e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133968" :question/problem "A teacher wants to determine whether a student's performance in mathematics influences their performance in physics. The following table shows the grades of $5$ students in a mathematics and physics class. \n\n| **Math Grade** | **$8$** | **$6$** | **$8$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Physics Grade** | $9$ | $5$ | $8$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?" :question/worked-solution "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (math grade) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (physics grade) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/5bdbaadf2d3ea794c145365f5ee61ee4c1551dc72b62c8a681933b9aac74d214.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f1049a-8af9-50ee-9dac-9dbd9c19bdc6" :knowledge-point/title "Correctly Identifying a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8d350d6-b4c4-5fba-ad23-09ccfb58082e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/726a22a7d72af2ba9a7b9c9568cc1723557ee8c0af4dd38a3dd9bacca4f72769.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247506} {:answer/id #uuid "f45365e7-f29c-5155-82a1-55f57b3dcb59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/8ea63450225d8b50e6f00e012afcd3afe8215eb573ed3a31ce9aa57c30ec8132.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247507} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2e0fa7-e574-56c0-886c-20f56e09891c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/b741264e080009d9e634e7ffce5e9041b6cd65b34e4d840700397a7378255ea8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247508} {:answer/id #uuid "b39fdbc2-18ec-597b-b8f8-61c6332beb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/81364754556cfeed2c4a2b74d2c745c0544