/13934290/assets/8088e41a66b4aba259d95f3099f71d5777caf876e9278e6b7f11c865ab12f7e0.png)\n\nTo determine the number of absences there were in a class whose size is $20$ students, we locate $20$ on the horizontal axis and move in the vertical direction until we find some points, as shown above.\n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(20,6).$ Therefore, there was a total of $6$ absences in the month for the class with $20$ students."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f99f2aa-f977-5d6e-ae62-a826a897ba9b" :knowledge-point/title "Reading a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53789f57-a1e1-5c99-a4bf-c67524e8f850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247548} {:answer/id #uuid "8d07cc59-2256-5267-aebc-3954c5f9211b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247549} {:answer/id #uuid "395efa17-97e0-5aba-bd63-fb823aec7554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247550} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd4c5ae-72cd-5ef6-9ae2-1e31a9e6b31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247551} {:answer/id #uuid "6913d9b1-a068-5fac-8005-f06aba6ee492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d07cc59-2256-5267-aebc-3954c5f9211b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247549} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab55777-109c-5426-9ba9-6cd9f63ef79e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247547}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb125bd9-7bea-58c1-8571-b6355117ef8d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134086" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/c93f14cd549ddbd849dfed5582bd4f414cf3eac95a4ba2c22d1d4014d3153980.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the number of absences in a month and the size of a class. What is the size of the class that had $7$ absences in the month?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/a41ff9a7f77a393b6575ee21525de15517038188afeca0b7783d175c3f4c34b1.png)\n\nTo determine the size of the class that had $7$ absences in a month, we locate $7$ on the vertical axis and move in the horizontal direction until we find some points, as shown above. \n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(16,7).$ Therefore, the class that had $7$ absences in the month has $16$ students."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f99f2aa-f977-5d6e-ae62-a826a897ba9b" :knowledge-point/title "Reading a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dabc0ef2-7d2d-57bd-863d-1782e8445cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247555} {:answer/id #uuid "86246c32-7325-5f1c-8b00-4aca62f9b80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247556} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e44b82-2383-571f-8f06-f5e14ed56b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247557} {:answer/id #uuid "e5dde166-6f84-564f-bdf6-fa442281dcf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247558} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e6a47f-59a8-5c70-ae1e-a1aa5a6a63c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "82%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86246c32-7325-5f1c-8b00-4aca62f9b80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247556} :answer-field/id #uuid "f66bf826-30e1-5333-a5a6-c7fbe26e9f82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247554}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cfd9a91-7414-56c2-8451-55d3c25c8cef" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134087" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/dc2f3fad9a09ed25fb9e6077069f63aac8afc09090f5453ece33c0b4ab5fb79f.png)\n\nA group of $10$ high school students is surveyed about their study habits. The scatter plot above shows the relationship between the amount of time they watch TV per week and their overall math scores. What is the overall math score of the student who watches TV for $10$ hours per week?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/500b2e9395d0af1b9ae86ce6e9b874b817690b61faad548c1fa9e33d495a5776.png)\n\nTo determine the overall math score of the student who watches TV for $10$ hours, we locate $10$ on the horizontal axis and move in the vertical direction until we find some points, as shown above.\n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(10,75).$ Therefore, the overall math score of the student who watches TV for $10$ hours per week is $75%.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247560 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "295f5dec-32aa-5bb8-8e35-3b058390c4c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247562} {:answer/id #uuid "a7539b53-6f66-5afd-b011-6507ad54ce73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247563} {:answer/id #uuid "f8dc7b12-58ec-51bb-842e-1dbc73c8020c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247564} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f00d4d-60fe-5e22-bdfa-72944431d9d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247565} {:answer/id #uuid "1af3cbfb-e55e-5dbf-bcd5-4591e707f871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8dc7b12-58ec-51bb-842e-1dbc73c8020c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247564} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbe62272-71d7-5da3-9f2e-a686a3433481" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247561}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df37bdae-6ef8-5470-898d-00206f96df51" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134105" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/5768d8f90d3dd754471a69d25582eca6cdb2f4993b9b22020dc9f2038aa61954.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above summarizes data collected by a Midwestern high school showing the relationship between the number of absences in a month and the class size. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one class reported a total of $6$ absences in the month.\n- Two classes have a total of $20$ students each.\n- Only one class has more than $24$ students." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is false. The scatter plot has two points whose vertical coordinate is equal to $6,$ namely, $(16,6)$ and $(20,6).$ This means that two of the classes each reported a total of 6 absences in the month.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/a62b1d5a63764b38013fdbdba9ba85a4495cd996a2d9f975dbe3d7eb89166234.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $20,$ namely, $(20,6).$ This means that only one of the classes has a total of  $20$ students.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/3c41f2e111ef141511ec4f2faa655ddcea8f2b7e0b73bd37f0b1e142d5d60f14.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. From the scatter plot, only one class has more than $24$ students. This class is represented by the point to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/adcba37370fdac69b152a8d18ef710d5f665d9a3252376ea312808be7d08a407.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baf0d4cb-7b0d-513d-aa07-81d47071b083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247569} {:answer/id #uuid "c56716ea-6860-57dd-9e78-481eec9697df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247570} {:answer/id #uuid "a94e25a0-f490-5d79-85c0-3d9885708946" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247571} {:answer/id #uuid "3eec39ee-49b2-5750-8425-9409c11897b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247572} {:answer/id #uuid "a3faf374-11a0-5f61-8756-5636fc0485b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c56716ea-6860-57dd-9e78-481eec9697df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247570} :answer-field/id #uuid "28a0c842-a781-5698-984d-f250f5c3dd45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247568}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28e73ddb-620f-53f5-9b92-ba2b12215281" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134128" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/69517e814dae28db96c64a662ce97b5fc40ea10355cb5a02561a0d12e1a3f845.png)\n\nA math teacher asked his students how many hours of sleep they had the\nnight before a test. The information he received is summarized in the scatter plot above.\n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one student obtained a score of $90.$\n- Only one student slept for $6$ hours.\n- None of the students obtained a score lower than $75.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $90,$ namely, $(7,90).$ This means that only one student obtained a score of $90.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/ef915015fa9c7685f45f26ee9cd2c10dfce5a4253aed22b6ea2ea57f0c3c26e2.png)\n\n    \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $6,$ namely, $(6,80)$ and $(6,85).$ This means that two students had  $6$ hours of sleep.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/3139ca71a780b76ca7355ddd119d6502f1cd390d67064db3a4a57801e33f2917.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, three students obtained a score lower than  $75.$  Those students are represented by the three dots below the horizontal line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/a675a94a9183a86d221bb2199dae38f9f55b9f91dff9868320b0b8f4d38b3fe9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9efe8a2-af82-54db-bef2-47217eb1d85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148999} {:answer/id #uuid "ea63764c-ad41-5a00-a5e2-128d4f53cb3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149000} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5be3cc-2571-5824-966a-18fe74eac1ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149001} {:answer/id #uuid "21d1a35f-f429-58bb-9cdb-6649f3eab00d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149002} {:answer/id #uuid "7a430968-e1ca-5f54-aaac-8b32bb26a033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a430968-e1ca-5f54-aaac-8b32bb26a033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149003} :answer-field/id #uuid "45871b81-94e6-596b-8f2a-6e55eb94474c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148998}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35f73958-c27b-5887-a2cc-b747d3896473" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134133" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2585/Source/Images/q-134133.png)\n\nMr. Clark recorded the height and shoe size of the players on the basketball team he coaches. The information he collected is summarized in the scatter plot above.\n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. Only one player has a shoe size of $9\\frac{1}{2}$.\n2. Only one player is $195cm$ tall.\n3. There are exactly two players taller than $185cm$." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose vertical coordinate equals $9.5,$ namely, $(180,9.5)$ and $(195,9.5).$ This means that two players have a shoe size of  $9\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/c2058bf02025ff359b509db01022c5d2e956d67243094a33692b90d6f1c2eac8.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement II is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $195,$ namely, $(195,\\,9.5).$ This means that only one of the players has a height of $195\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/b8b4364dc5de11eed12840bc644b1392b36160adfdf739b96f282c2367d999fa.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement III is false. According to the scatter diagram, three players have a height greater than  $185\\,\\text{cm},$ represented by the three dots to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/aaf6d496c56c3cdc5a47e1c09e7640d7a3caa05446a75b705c042a56c116cb98.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3564eea-7797-54b8-acb8-a0e7c84860fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247576} {:answer/id #uuid "8d321eb8-847f-5122-990d-9e51d6ce8913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247577} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd8381b-575b-57e1-a055-6d0b109a4637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247578} {:answer/id #uuid "acc5bf35-548f-546f-9760-36c31a650f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247579} {:answer/id #uuid "a120b98f-8d5c-5fc8-b135-d8787a810ff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d321eb8-847f-5122-990d-9e51d6ce8913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247577} :answer-field/id #uuid "8969df3b-9e06-59cd-a66b-83c1ff53cb37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247575}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5695618-d5cd-597b-aa17-57a1d31983f4" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134139" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/376bd65db6b1d0a91c6013462e686ffad4d8acceee4948e61cf291d6403a12cd.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above is based on data collected from several homes in a given community. It shows the relationship between the age of a house and the number of people living in it. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There is only one house where precisely $3$ people live.\n- Two of the houses are $16$ years old.\n- Only one house is older than $24$ years old." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $3,$ namely, $(18,3).$ This means that there is only one house where $3$ people live.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/7a56236f0c5649a64436809b2a5e1fb8f00ed3d345cd81c571f96d579d6c19b6.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $16,$ namely, $(16,6).$ This means that only one house is $16$ years old.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/6d9a60cd10c6d7cc9f9d51d0be44c32cb688e19da988b3e84b30f0c4be32a2a8.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, two houses are more than $24$ years old, represented by the two dots to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/44b7395bb2e5ee0a71899869e6caedb949e8744adde314134f6a09e4c8f8a35d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}]}
